      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64315,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 294,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tunnel clusters are usually asymptomatic but can occasionally cause a mucoid discharge {2206083}. They rarely may present as a clinically visible mass {8898835}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:00:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64316,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 294,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tunnel clusters are generally incidental findings that affect about 10% of adult women, usually multiparous {2206083; 13700409}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:00:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64317,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 294,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:00:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64318,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 294,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The association with multiparity suggests that tunnel clusters may represent involutional change within endocervical glandular hyperplasia {2206083}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:00:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64319,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 294,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>About 40% of cases of the cystic variety show a grossly visible, lobulated lesion, with a mean size of 2.4&nbsp;mm {2206083}. They are multiple in 80% of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:00:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64320,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 294,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tunnel clusters consist of rounded, lobular aggregates of closely packed endocervical-lined tubules of varying size. Non-cystic tunnel clusters show predominantly small glands, whereas cystic tunnel clusters show dilated glands. The lining consists of flattened cuboidal or columnar cells. Atypia and mitotic activity are generally absent but rarely can be noted {13700409; 8898835}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:00:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64321,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 294,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:00:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
